WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.013
<v Krista>In this video,</v>

2
00:00:01.013 --> 00:00:02.530
we're talking about division of radicals

3
00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:04.660
or division of square roots.

4
00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:07.148
And when we're dealing with division of radicals,

5
00:00:07.148 --> 00:00:09.010
the formula we need to remember

6
00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:11.540
is that the square root of A over the square root of B,

7
00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:13.490
in other words, when we have a fraction

8
00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:14.790
with a square root in the numerator

9
00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.620
and a square root in the denominator,

10
00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:19.350
we can combine those into one square root

11
00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:22.940
and just use A over B inside of the square root.

12
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:24.050
So, in this first example here,

13
00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:27.290
we have the square root of 100 over the square root of 4.

14
00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:29.110
There's a couple ways we can go about this.

15
00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:30.430
Using the formula here,

16
00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:34.440
we can say that this is equal to the square root of 100

17
00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.430
over 4, in other words, we can take the values here

18
00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:39.133
and put them inside one square root

19
00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:41.160
instead of two square roots.

20
00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:43.480
And then, we would just simplify the fraction inside.

21
00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:47.590
So, we know that 100 over 4 is equal to 25.

22
00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:50.480
So, this would simplify to the square root of 25,

23
00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.790
because we simplify 100 over 4.

24
00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:55.270
And then, from here, we just take the square root of 25,

25
00:00:55.270 --> 00:00:57.310
and we know that that's equal to 5.

26
00:00:57.310 --> 00:00:58.750
So, we could do it that way,

27
00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:01.240
or we could deal with each square root separately.

28
00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.876
So instead of bringing one hundred and four

29
00:01:03.876 --> 00:01:07.270
into one square root, we can deal with them individually.

30
00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:10.040
So we know that the square root of 100 is 10,

31
00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:11.800
so we end up with 10 here.

32
00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:13.920
We know that the square root of 4 is 2,

33
00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:15.900
so we'd have 2 and we could say that 10 over 2

34
00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:17.153
is equal to 5.

35
00:01:17.153 --> 00:01:19.780
Notice that in both cases we get the same answer,

36
00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:20.950
we always get 5.

37
00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:22.670
That's because it's going to work either way

38
00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:24.500
as long as we do the math correctly.

39
00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:26.290
So whatever's easiest for you,

40
00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:27.930
deal with the square root separately

41
00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:30.420
and then do the division of whole numbers here

42
00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.460
or pull both numbers into a fraction

43
00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:33.900
inside of one square root

44
00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.660
and then simplify that fraction taking

45
00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:37.750
the square root later.

46
00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:39.400
So again, two ways you can go about it.

47
00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:40.910
Let's look at a second example.

48
00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:42.440
We have the square root of 24

49
00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:44.740
over the square root of 18.

50
00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:47.170
Let's go ahead and deal with the square roots separately.

51
00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:49.460
So if we look at the square root of 24 here,

52
00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:50.930
we know that that's the same thing

53
00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:54.510
as the square root of 6 times 4,

54
00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:56.249
because 6 times 4 is 24,

55
00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:58.440
so really we just have the square root of 24

56
00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:00.180
we haven't changed anything.

57
00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.550
In the denominator here we have the square root of 18,

58
00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:06.000
which we can say is the square root of 6 times 3.

59
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.620
6 times 3 is 18 so we just have the square root

60
00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:11.240
of 18, we haven't changed anything there either.

61
00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:13.380
Now we need to remember the square root rule,

62
00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.210
that tells us that if we have the square root

63
00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:18.600
of A times B under one square root,

64
00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:20.210
we can change that to the square root

65
00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:22.700
of A times the square root of B.

66
00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:24.870
In other words we have two values multiplied together

67
00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:26.340
underneath one square root,

68
00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:28.650
we can pull them out into their own square roots.

69
00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:31.370
So what this becomes then is the square root

70
00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:33.700
of 6 times the square root of 4,

71
00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:36.050
we separate 6 and 4 into their own

72
00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:37.680
square roots in the numerator,

73
00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:39.600
